-- title:
--   Degree of the Γ_H level field over L(j(q^{qℓ}))
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79); that is, $K$ is the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`, where `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$. Let $y\in K$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), i.e. the series obtained from the $q$-expansion `jqModC L` $=\mathfrak q^{-1}\cdot(\text{integral }j\text{-numerator})$ by the substitution $\mathfrak q\mapsto \mathfrak q^{q\ell}$. Then the $L(y)$-dimension of $K$, where $L(y)$ is the intermediate field generated by $y$, equals $\bigl(\prod_{p\mid M'}p^{v_p(M')-1}(p+1)\bigr)\cdot q(q^2-1)\cdot\ell(\ell^2-1)/2$, the division being division of natural numbers.
--
--   This is the degree of the level field attached to $\Gamma_H \subseteq \Gamma_0((q\ell)^2M')$ over the rational subfield generated by the moduli parameter $j$ of the Tate curve at the $q\ell$-th power of the uniformiser, the function-field form of the classical degree computation for $X_H \to X(1)$; the right-hand side is $\psi(M')\,|\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q)|\,|\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{F}_\ell)|/2$. It is used in the computation of the rank of a fraction-ring tensor product in the full-level classification, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.finrank_fractionRing_tensorProduct_quotient_ker_classify_eq_of_dense_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.finrank_fractionRing_tensorProduct_quotient_ker_classify_eq_of_dense_gamma0Pow).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField_levelH_eq.lean

